### Sprite Sheet Alignment & Phaser 3 Implementation Summary

I have re-processed all character sprite sheets to fix frame alignment and documented the Phaser 3 origin/pivot implementation:

---

### 1. Sprite Slicing & Baseline Alignment Fix ([`scripts/slice_characters.py`](file:///Users/atarzwell/src/dhaul4/scripts/slice_characters.py))

- **Bounding Box Trimming:** Added automatic non-transparent bounding-box extraction (`rgba_img.getbbox()`) for every individual frame across all 4 haulers (Gnome, Sprite, Halfling, Dwarf).
- **Ground Contact Baseline:** Character feet are now anchored to **`y = 44`** within the standard 48×48 px cell.
- **Horizontal Center:** Character torsos are aligned to **`x = 24`** (horizontal mid-point).
- **Result:** Re-built all 4 WebP texture atlases (`char_gnome`, `char_sprite`, `char_halfling`, `char_dwarf`) in `client/public/assets/atlases/`. Animation loops (`Idle`, `Run`, `Jump`, `Duck`, `Hurt`, `Stunned`) now play in the asset gallery lightbox modal with zero vertical jitter or horizontal drifting.

---

### 2. Phaser 3 Developer Implementation Guide ([`docs/art/PIPELINE-AND-PHASER-GUIDE.md`](file:///Users/atarzwell/src/dhaul4/docs/art/PIPELINE-AND-PHASER-GUIDE.md#L104-L125))

Added Section 3.1.1 specifying how the game presentation engine (C-02) should configure character sprites:

```typescript
// Recommended Phaser 3 Character Initialization
const player = scene.physics.add.sprite(x, y, 'char_gnome', 'char_gnome_idle_0');

// 1. Set Bottom-Center Origin (aligns feet to ground baseline)
player.setOrigin(0.5, 1.0); 

// 2. Set Physics Body Hitbox
player.body.setSize(24, 40);   // 24x40 px physics box
player.body.setOffset(12, 4);   // Centered horizontally inside 48x48 cell

// 3. Stack Mount Anchor Offset (for stacked loot above head)
const CARRY_STACK_OFFSET_Y = -44;
```

